ooks wired to this one","color":"#8C93AD","s":-2,"n":1,"y":560,"h":100}],"portalHeaders":[{"code":"1TH","name":"1 Thessalonians","slug":"1-thessalonians","live":true,"x":44,"y":629}],"portalColor":{"OT":"#8C93AD","NT":"#D8DCEB"},"groups":[{"label":"Creation","color":"#7FB77E"},{"label":"Noah","color":"#4EA8DE"},{"label":"Abraham","color":"#D9A441"},{"label":"Moses","color":"#C05746"},{"label":"David","color":"#B07CD4"},{"label":"New covenant","color":"#E4DFCE"},{"label":"Unassigned","color":"#5A6178"}],"relkinds":[{"key":"quoted-in","label":"Quoted in","color":"#E8C15A","strong":true},{"key":"fulfilled-in","label":"Fulfilled in","color":"#D9715C","strong":true},{"key":"parallels","label":"Parallels","color":"#6E9BD1","strong":false},{"key":"illustrates-doctrine","label":"Illustrates doctrine","color":"#9B8AD1","strong":false},{"key":"part-of-covenant","label":"Part of covenant","color":"#5FBFA0","strong":false}],"counts":{"topics":6,"portals":1,"edges":6,"relations":0,"outbound":0},"nodes":[{"id":"bt_2th_judgment_relief","p":0,"x":56,"y":239,"s":0,"g":6,"bk":"2TH","ty":"DOCTRINE","t":"Persecution, God's righteous judgment and Christ revealed","d":"Paul thanks God for their growing faith under persecution and says God will repay those who trouble them and give rest to believers when the Lord Jesus is revealed from heaven.","q":"Can {{name}} explain what Paul says will happen when the Lord Jesus is revealed from heaven (1:7-10)?","ev":["State what 1:6-7 says God will do for the troubled and for those who trouble them","Describe how Christ is revealed in 1:7-10"],"pp":[[52,1,1,12]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_book_2th","p":0,"x":56,"y":109,"s":-1,"g":6,"bk":"2TH","ty":"BOOK_OVERVIEW","t":"2 Thessalonians: overview","d":"Paul's second letter to the Thessalonians on persecution and God's judgment (ch. 1), the day of Christ and the man of sin (ch. 2), and prayer, work and discipline (ch. 3).","q":"Can {{name}} explain in a few sentences what 2 Thessalonians is about?","ev":["Describe the three movements: judgment and relief (1), the day of Christ (2), prayer and work (3)"],"pp":[[52,1,1,12],[52,2,1,17],[52,3,1,18]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_2th_man_of_sin","p":0,"x":56,"y":369,"s":1,"g":6,"bk":"2TH","ty":"DOCTRINE","t":"The day of Christ and the man of sin","d":"Paul tells them not to be shaken as if the day of Christ had come, because a falling away and the revealing of the man of sin come first, whom the Lord will destroy at his coming.","q":"Can {{name}} explain why Paul says the Thessalonians should not be troubled that the day of Christ is at hand (2:1-3)?","ev":["Say what must come before that day (2:3)","State what happens to the Wicked when the Lord comes (2:8)"],"pp":[[52,2,1,12]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_2th_chosen_stand_fast","p":0,"x":244,"y":369,"s":1,"g":6,"bk":"2TH","ty":"DOCTRINE","t":"Chosen to salvation: stand fast","d":"Paul gives thanks that God chose them from the beginning to salvation through sanctification and belief of the truth, and tells them to hold the teachings they received and prays for their comfort.","q":"Can {{name}} explain what Paul says God has done for the Thessalonians in 2:13-14?","ev":["Name the means of salvation in 2:13","Tell what Paul tells them to hold in 2:15"],"pp":[[52,2,13,17]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_2th_prayer_request","p":0,"x":56,"y":499,"s":2,"g":6,"bk":"2TH","ty":"THEME","t":"Pray for us; the Lord is faithful","d":"Paul asks prayer that the word of the Lord run freely and that they be delivered from wicked men, and affirms that the Lord is faithful to establish and keep them.","q":"Can {{name}} say what Paul asks the Thessalonians to pray for, and who he says is faithful (3:1-3)?","ev":["State the two requests of 3:1-2","Find who is faithful in 3:3"],"pp":[[52,3,1,5]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_2th_idleness","p":0,"x":244,"y":499,"s":2,"g":6,"bk":"2TH","ty":"THEME","t":"Work, and dealing with the disorderly","d":"Paul commands them to withdraw from brothers who live disorderly and will not work, pointing to his own example of labour, and says to admonish such a person as a brother, not treat him as an enemy.","q":"Can {{name}} explain what example Paul set about work and what he told them to do about those who would not work (3:7-12)?","ev":["Quote or paraphrase 3:10 and say who it addresses","Explain how the disorderly are to be treated (3:14-15)"],"pp":[[52,3,6,18]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_1th_day_of_lord","p":1,"x":244,"y":629,"s":-2,"g":6,"bk":"1TH","ty":"DOCTRINE","t":"The day of the Lord and living as children of the day","d":"The day of the Lord comes as a thief in the night on those who say peace and safety, but believers, children of light, are to be watchful and sober, since God appointed them to salvation.","q":"Can {{name}} explain why Paul says believers are not in darkness that the day should overtake them as a thief (5:4-5)?","ev":["Contrast night and day in 5:4-8","Name the armour in 5:8"],"pp":[[51,5,1,11]],"tier":null}],"edges":[[0,6,0],[2,0,1],[3,2,0],[4,3,0],[5,4,0],[1,0,0]],"rel":[]}
